in cana bridge of spirits everyday items  are imbued with emotional significance a  wooden mask is a link to the spirit of  the person it was made for objects like  a hammer or a box of food are tied to  memories of people who have been lost  locations that were once the sites of  happy times are scarred with the pain  and trauma suffered within them looking  at common things with new eyes is a  running theme of kana and that theme  often applies to its gameplay as well  though the game is filled with some  fairly common action-adventure genre  tropes it has melee combat and climbing  similar to games such as star wars jedi  fallen order or even sakuro shadows die  twice platforming that recalls games  such as ratchet and clank and puzzles  like you might see in the legend of  zelda it manages to combine a familiar  approachability with some fresh spins on  the ideas those elements combine with  emotional character-driven storytelling  some tough but excellent fights and  mechanics that make the world feel alive  around you  the story and world of cana bridge of  spirits center on a village beset by  tragedy its inhabitants are all gone  wiped out by misfortune and their pain  has manifested as poison in the once  vibrant land around it that pain has  drawn cana a young spirit guide to seek  out the trauma at its center and heal it  while also searching for answers to her  own personal tragedy  i sense suffering here spirit  do you need help her link to the spirit  realm allows her to interact with the  ghosts of the past and to help them find  peace and in so doing she's able to push  back the corruption that has gripped the  land restoring it to its former glory  you do that by wandering the village and  its surrounding environs battling the  corrupted spirits of both the people who  once lived there and the nature their  pain has twisted most every interaction  comes down to a combination of combat  and puzzle solving your goal is usually  to beat down some enemies freeing up the  ability to destroy a nearby corrupted  heart with a blast of spirit energy you  can pulse from kana with the touch of a  button kill the heart and the corruption  recedes along with the corrupted enemies  combat is mostly familiar with kana  fighting off enemies with the use of her  spirit staff you get light and heavy  attacks you can combo together but even  in normal difficulty enemies hit hard  and can knock you off your game if  you're not paying attention like similar  action games you have a dodge to avoid  attacks with the right timing and a  shield that will stop most blows take  too many hits and the shield breaks  sending you flying and dealing you  damage but if you can time your block  just right you'll parry an enemy and  open them up to a counter-attack  both kana's puzzles and its combat add a  twist in the form of the rot which are  little spirit pals you can find in the  environment the rot are a bit like  pikmin or the minions in games such as  overlord in combat you can send them to  attack or distract enemies and you need  their help to destroy hearts which can  stop more enemies from respawning the  rot are the thing that makes kana stand  apart from similar games and using them  effectively adds a tactical layer to  fights since the rot are all pretty  small you need to work up their courage  to bring them into a battle as you deal  damage and kill enemies you fill a meter  that gives you a rot action  and you can send them out with a single  button or use them to power up one of  your attacks for a big hit the rot are  also crucial for taking advantage of the  environment to destroy hearts or to heal  kana working with the rot in combat  forces you to constantly be on the  attack and to pay attention to your  environment it's often essential that  you knock out smaller weaker enemies to  build rot charges so you can distract  and take down bigger tougher ones  deciding how best to use the rot in  combat keeps you balancing a big picture  view of the fight with the smaller more  intense moments of parrying a hit or  sniping a weak point occasionally the  combination of those elements can be a  bit annoying because it's easy to miss a  single dodge or block and have tough  enemies lay into you or to accidentally  send the rot to attack the wrong enemy  as things get hectic with some bosses  you'll probably need to die a few times  just to figure out how badly they're  capable of wrecking you but the game is  always quick to get you back into the  action with as little punishment as  possible it also offers a story mode  difficulty which seems like a very good  addition given how deceptively difficult  some of its fights can be heinous combat  is generally tough and exciting  executing well on familiar dodge and  parry mechanics but it's the addition of  the rot and the versatility and how you  can use them that really makes fighting  in kana feel fun and intelligent that  also goes for the game's various puzzles  outside of combat the rot can be sent to  do contextual actions in the world like  moving climbable objects to help you  reach a high platform kana does a good  job of combining the need to give the  rot commands with smart uses of kana's  abilities creating situations in which  solutions need you to think about what  you can do with your unlockable bow or  platform levitating bombs as well as  what the rot can do to alter the  environment it never gets too complex  but it's enough to make you feel like  you're doing a lot as you explore  where kanan nails the balance is in  providing you with tons of little  puzzles that mostly reward your  observation skills without overly taxing  your ability to solve them most of the  time spotting something the rot can move  or seeing an object you can interact  with using spirit energy is enough to  illuminate the path forward or some  hidden secret kana is also brimming with  collectibles including hidden rot  spirits and hats to customize them  chasing those items isn't essential but  the addition of all those little side  paths and tiny rewards encourages you to  explore and lose yourself in cana's  world and it is a beautiful world to  explore thanks to the phenomenal art  direction and an excellent immersive  score and made more so by the stories of  the spirits found within it the game is  full of cute characters and gorgeous  cutscenes that help to invest you even  further in uncovering what has happened  in the village and setting it right in  each section of the game you venture out  to find one particular tormented spirit  and help them achieve peace and your  journey through the location is all  about piecing together the story of who  these people are and what became of them  your interactions with the characters  you find in each section of the game  helps imbue the areas in and around the  village with a character all their own  easy there old friend  i'm happy to see you too  what's missing from the story though is  kana herself the game hints that some  tragedy in kana's past has scarred her  much like the spirit she sets out to  help but the game never really spends  too much time on her history and it  seems like some of those plot threads  are left dangling in a game where so  much development is given to the stories  of the inhabitants of the village it  doesn't feel like enough attention is  paid to kana by comparison the act of  meeting and understanding all those  other characters is powerful though k9  bridge of spirits is a game about making  those connections just like it's about  making a connection with the game world  around you through the rod  it's about exploring a world and seeing  what it once was and helping to restore  it to be that again and while cana  bridge of spirits is full of familiar  feeling combat and exploration its  ability to find different ways to look  at those ideas makes for a beautiful  emotional and exciting journey  [Music]
 

